 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Hands for «خذ العفو», geometric for «فاستعذ بالله». The Shaytan is not drawn. STAGING v4: 199-200 are addressed to the Prophet; Al-Muyassar says to him and his community, As-Sa'di says it is how one deals with people, so the believers (a group of three, never a lone man) act it and the Prophet is never shown or implied. c1 (199) is a market street: a rude man points at the believers (199:1, As-Sa'di: whoever harms you by word or deed), they answer with good words (199:3, enjoin what is good; a lamp plate on 199:4) and turn away from him (199:5, turn away from the ignorant), the camera then closes on the believers (199:6) so the rude man is out of frame when the next verse, about the Shaytan, begins. c2 (200): the believers sit at home; the Shaytan is never drawn and nothing stands for him (camera only on 200:1-5); they raise their hands on 200:6 (seek refuge, As-Sa'di: take shelter with Allah), with a geometric plate from 200:6 over the Name and the two attributes."
 },
